# SMART scope builder of an app (crate::idp::scopes, idp-scopes.js) and the
# "How SMART access works" explainer. %name% placeholders are filled in by
# the script; { $name } ones by the server.

idps-lede = Scopes decide what kinds of data the app may ask for. Which patients a user can open is set on each user's Resource access.
idps-how-link = How SMART access works
idps-copy-lines = One per line
idps-copy-space = Space-separated (scope parameter)
idps-presets = Start from a preset
idps-preset-patient-read = Patient-facing, read-only
idps-preset-patient-read-desc = A patient signs in, picks their record, and the app reads it. Stays signed in.
idps-preset-clinician-read = Clinician, read-only
idps-preset-clinician-read-desc = A clinician reads everything they may see, launched from the EHR.
idps-preset-clinician-write = Clinician, read and write
idps-preset-clinician-write-desc = Like read-only, plus create, update and delete.
idps-preset-ehr-launch = EHR launch
idps-preset-ehr-launch-desc = Opened from the EHR with the current patient; reads that patient's data.
idps-preset-backend-export = Backend bulk export
idps-preset-backend-export-desc = A server without a user reads everything (client_credentials only).
idps-preset-identity = Identity only
idps-preset-identity-desc = Sign the user in and learn who they are; no FHIR data.

